const e=JSON.parse(`[{"set_id":"LR_E20_S1_8","exercise":"exercise_1","type":"selection_criteria_decision","is_set":true,"setup_text":"Directions for questions 1 to 8: Study the following information carefully and answer the questions given below.\\n\\nA reputed FMCG Company decided to recruit a marketing manager for their operations in India. The candidate must\\n(i) be an Indian citizen.\\n(ii) be a graduate with a minimum of 60% marks.\\n(iii) have done an M.B.A or a diploma course in Marketing with a minimum of 55% marks.\\n(iv) have at least two years experience in an FMCG company as a marketing manager.\\n(v) be not less than 25 years of age and not more than 30 years as on 01.01.2005.\\n\\nHowever, if a candidate fulfils all other criteria except\\n(P) condition (ii) above but has secured 65% marks or more in M.B.A and also has at least three years experience as a marketing manager in an FMCG company, then he is referred to the Chairman.\\n(Q) condition (iii) above but has an experience of over 5 years as a marketing manager in an FMCG company, he is to be selected.\\n(R) condition (iv) above but has done his M.B.A from a reputed institution with more than 60% of marks, he is considered for the post of a probationary marketing officer.\\n\\nBased on the above criteria and information provided against each candidate take a decision in each case. You are not to assume anything. If the data given is not adequate to take a decision, mark your answer as data inadequate. Give answer\\n(A) if the candidate is to be selected or is to be rejected.\\n(B) if the candidate is to be referred to the chairman.\\n(C) if the candidate is considered for the post of a probationary marketing officer.\\n(D) if data is inadequate.","setup_solution":"Each candidate is checked against the five mandatory criteria (i)-(v). Note that answer (A) covers BOTH 'selected' and 'rejected' outcomes, so missing data about a no-exception criterion (i or v) does not create genuine ambiguity as long as it doesn't change which of A/B/C/D applies. If exactly one of (ii),(iii),(iv) fails, the corresponding exception (P/Q/R) is checked; if it applies, the answer is B or C instead of A. If two or more criteria fail simultaneously, no exception applies. If a missing data point could push the answer to two genuinely different codes, the answer is data inadequate (D).","entity_count":8,"variables":[],"constraints":[],"case_splits":[],"resolution_type":"rule_based_decision","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["criteria_checklist_evaluation","exception_handling","data_sufficiency_analysis"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E20_Q001","question_text":"Sravan, an Indian citizen was 28 years of old as on 25th July 2004. He has secured 65% marks in the graduation and 58% marks in M.B.A. He is working in an FMCG company as a marketing manager for the last three years.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected/Rejected","solution_text":"Indian citizen (i). Age 28 as on 25-Jul-2004, so still 28 as on 01-01-2005 - within 25-30 (v). Graduation 65%>=60% (ii). MBA 58%>=55% (iii). 3 years as marketing manager in FMCG >=2 years (iv). All 5 mandatory criteria satisfied -> Selected (both selected and rejected outcomes map to answer A).","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q002","question_text":"Ashank has secured 68% marks in his graduation. He is an Indian citizen, 29 years old as on 5th November 2004 and is working as a marketing manager in an FMCG company since 1st April 1997.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected/Rejected","solution_text":"Citizen (i), age 29 as on 01-01-2005 (v), graduation 68% (ii) all satisfied. Experience as marketing manager since 1997 is roughly 7-8 years (iv, far exceeds 2 years). MBA/diploma marks (iii) are not stated: if he meets (iii) he is selected outright; if he fails (iii), exception Q applies (fails iii alone, but has over 5 years experience as marketing manager in FMCG - he has ~7-8 years) -> selected. Both branches give 'selected' (answer A), so the missing data does not create genuine ambiguity.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q003","question_text":"Vijay Varma was born on 12th August 1977. He secured 65% and 60% marks in his graduation and M.B.A. respectively. He has been working as a marketing manager in an FMCG company for the last three years.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected/Rejected","solution_text":"Age ~27 as on 01-01-2005 (v), graduation 65% (ii), MBA 60% (iii), 3 years experience (iv) all satisfied. Indian citizenship (i) is never stated, but condition (i) has no exception clause: if he is a citizen he is selected, if not he is rejected - both outcomes map to answer A ('selected/rejected'). Not genuinely ambiguous.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q004","question_text":"Pranay is an Indian citizen born in 1978. He completed his M.B.A with 68% marks and has been working in an FMCG company for the last four years.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Citizen (i), age ~26-27 as on 01-01-2005 (v), MBA 68% (iii), 4 years as marketing manager in FMCG (iv) all satisfied. Graduation marks (ii) are not stated. If graduation >=60%, he is selected (answer A). If graduation <60%, exception P applies (fails ii alone, MBA>=65% [68% yes] and >=3 years experience as marketing manager [4 yes]) -> referred to Chairman (answer B). Since these are genuinely different answer codes (A vs B), the missing data makes this data inadequate.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q005","question_text":"Sri Vidya, an Indian girl born in 1976, has completed her graduation with 72% marks and her M.B.A. with 58% marks and has been working in an FMCG company for the last 6 months.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected/Rejected","solution_text":"Citizen, age, graduation 72% (ii), MBA 58%>=55% (iii) all satisfied. Only 6 months experience (iv) fails the 2-year minimum. Exception R requires MBA from a reputed institution with >60% marks; her MBA is 58%, not >60%, so exception R does not apply -> rejected (answer A, since selected/rejected share the same code).","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q006","question_text":"Anirudh, an Indian citizen born in 1978, has a consistent academic record with more than 70% marks. He did his M.B.A from a reputed institution and he has no experience as a marketing manager.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","solution_text":"'Consistent academic record with more than 70% marks' is read as both graduation and MBA exceeding 70% (ii, iii, and the >60% MBA threshold of exception R). He has zero experience as a marketing manager, failing (iv) alone. Since his MBA is from a reputed institution with >60% marks, exception R applies -> considered for probationary marketing officer (C).","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q007","question_text":"Rahul who was born in 1977, has completed both his graduation and M.B.A with 60% marks and has been working as a marketing manager with an FMCG company for the last three years.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected/Rejected","solution_text":"Age ~27-28 as on 01-01-2005 (v, within range regardless of exact birth month), graduation 60% meets the 'minimum 60%' threshold (ii), MBA 60%>=55% (iii), 3 years experience (iv) all satisfied. Indian citizenship (i) is not stated, but as with Q3, both possible outcomes (selected if citizen, rejected if not) map to the same answer code A.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q008","question_text":"Sourav, is 27 years old as on 23.07.03, and has completed his graduation with 62% marks and has a diploma in Marketing with 60% marks. He has been working as a marketing manager for 3 years with one of the leading FMCG company and he is an Indian citizen.","options":{"A":"Selected/Rejected","B":"Referred to Chairman","C":"Considered for probationary marketing officer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected/Rejected","solution_text":"Citizen (i), age ~28-29 as on 01-01-2005 (v), graduation 62% (ii), diploma 60%>=55% (iii), 3 years experience (iv) - all criteria met. Selected (answer A).","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E20_S9_16","exercise":"exercise_1","type":"selection_criteria_decision","is_set":true,"setup_text":"Directions for questions 9 to 16: Study the following information carefully and answer the questions given below.\\n\\nFollowing is the criteria for granting admission to the candidates into the post-graduate course in Fashion Technology. The candidate must\\n(i) have completed graduation in Fashion Technology, with at least 60% marks.\\n(ii) not be more than 30 years of age as on 01.06.2004.\\n(iii) have obtained at least 50% marks in the entrance examination.\\n(iv) pay a sum of Rs.50,000 at the time of admission as course fee.\\n\\nHowever, if a candidate fulfils all the other criteria except\\n(P) condition (i) above but has secured minimum 50% marks in graduation in Fashion Technology and can pay an amount of Rs.1,00,000 (including the course fee) towards development fund, he is referred to the Chairman.\\n(Q) condition (ii) above but is less than 35 years old and has at least three years of industry experience, he is referred to the Principal.\\n(R) condition (iii) above but has secured more than 75% marks in the graduation in Fashion Technology, he is referred to the Principal.\\n(S) condition (iv) above but can pay Rs.5000 per month for all the twelve months in an academic year, he is referred to the Chairman.\\n\\nBased on the above criteria and information provided for each candidate, take a decision in each case. You are not to assume anything. If the data given is not adequate to take a decision, mark your answer as data inadequate. Give answer\\n(A) if the candidate is to be admitted.\\n(B) if the candidate is to be referred to the Chairman or the principal.\\n(C) if the data is inadequate.\\n(D) if the candidate is to be rejected.","setup_solution":"Each candidate is checked against the four mandatory criteria (i)-(iv). Unlike Q1-8, admitted (A) and rejected (D) are separate codes here, so missing data about any mandatory criterion can create genuine ambiguity. If exactly one criterion fails, the corresponding exception (P/Q/R/S) is checked.","entity_count":8,"variables":[],"constraints":[],"case_splits":[],"resolution_type":"rule_based_decision","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["criteria_checklist_evaluation","exception_handling","data_sufficiency_analysis"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E20_Q009","question_text":"Vivek has completed his graduation in Fashion Technology with more than 50%. He was 28 years of age as on 01.01.2004. He scored 60% in the entrance test and is ready to pay Rs.50,000.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Age ~28 as on 01.06.2004 (ii, <=30 ok). Entrance test 60%>=50% (iii). Fee 50,000 (iv). Graduation in Fashion Technology is stated only as 'more than 50%', which does not confirm whether it meets the required 60% threshold (i). If >=60%, he is admitted (A). If between 50-60%, condition (i) fails; exception P requires >=50% graduation AND ability to pay Rs.1,00,000 towards development fund - he can only pay Rs.50,000, so exception P's payment condition is not met, and he would be rejected (D). Since A and D are different codes, this is genuinely data inadequate.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q010","question_text":"Ratur has completed his graduation in Fashion Technology with 62% marks and cleared the entrance test with 55% marks. He was born in 1976 and can pay the stipulated amount of Rs.50,000.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Admitted","solution_text":"Graduation 62%>=60% (i). Entrance test 55%>=50% (iii). Born 1976, so ~28 as on 01.06.2004, within the <=30 limit (ii). Pays Rs.50,000 (iv). All 4 criteria satisfied -> Admitted.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q011","question_text":"D'Souza, a 27 years old girl as on 1st January 2003, has completed her graduation in Fashion Technology with 55% of marks and cleared the entrance test with the same percentage of marks. She is ready to pay the amount of one lakh towards development fund.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","solution_text":"As on 01.01.2003 she is 27, so as on 01.06.2004 (~1.4 years later) she is 28-29, still <=30 (ii). Entrance test 55%>=50% (iii). Graduation 55% fails the 60% requirement (i). She can pay Rs.1,00,000 towards development fund, matching exception P exactly (fails i alone, has >=50% in Fashion Technology graduation, and can pay Rs.1,00,000 including course fee) -> referred to the Chairman.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q012","question_text":"Ujjal who was born in 1971, has completed his graduation in Fashion Technology with 60% of marks and scored 62% of marks in the entrance test. He has been working as a Fashion Designer for the last 4 years and he can pay the admission fee of Rs.50,000.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","solution_text":"Born 1971, so ~33 as on 01.06.2004, failing the <=30 age limit (ii). Graduation 60% (i), entrance test 62% (iii), fee Rs.50,000 (iv) all satisfied. Exception Q: fails (ii) alone, but is <35 years (33<35) and has >=3 years industry experience (4 years as Fashion Designer >=3) -> referred to the Principal.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q013","question_text":"Girish has completed his graduation with 70% marks and was born in 1978. He got 60% in the entrance test and is ready to pay the fee of Rs.50,000 at the time of admission.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Admitted","solution_text":"Graduation 70%>=60% (i). Born 1978, so ~26 as on 01.06.2004, within <=30 (ii). Entrance test 60%>=50% (iii). Fee Rs.50,000 (iv). All 4 criteria satisfied -> Admitted.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q014","question_text":"Sri Vidya has completed her graduation in Fashion Technology with 85% marks and she is the topper in the entrance test. She is 28 years old as on 1-6-2004, but she cannot pay any fee.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Rejected","solution_text":"Graduation 85%>=60% (i). Topper in entrance test implies well above 50% (iii). Age 28 as on 01.06.2004 (ii). She cannot pay any fee at all, failing (iv) outright. Exception S requires ability to pay Rs.5000/month for all 12 months (Rs.60,000/year); since she cannot pay anything, this condition is also not met -> exception S does not apply -> Rejected.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q015","question_text":"Karthikeyan a 27 year old as on 1-6-2003, has completed his graduation in Fashion Technology with 55% marks and he scored 58% in the entrance test. He is ready to pay the fee of Rs.1 lakh towards development fund.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","solution_text":"27 as on 01.06.2003, so 28 as on 01.06.2004, within <=30 (ii). Entrance test 58%>=50% (iii). Graduation 55% fails the 60% requirement (i). He can pay Rs.1,00,000 towards development fund, exactly matching exception P (fails i alone, >=50% graduation, can pay Rs.1,00,000 including course fee) -> referred to the Chairman.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q016","question_text":"Akash Deep has completed his graduation in Fashion Technology with 62% marks and has cleared the entrance test with 57% marks. He is 26 years old by 1st July 2003 and can pay Rs.50,000, at the time of admission.","options":{"A":"Admitted","B":"Referred to Chairman/Principal","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Admitted","solution_text":"Graduation 62%>=60% (i). Entrance test 57%>=50% (iii). 26 as on 01.07.2003, so ~26-27 as on 01.06.2004, within <=30 (ii). Fee Rs.50,000 (iv). All 4 criteria satisfied -> Admitted.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E20_S17_24","exercise":"exercise_1","type":"selection_criteria_decision","is_set":true,"setup_text":"Directions for questions 17 to 24: Study the following information carefully and answer the questions given below.\\n\\nIndusland a leading BPO decided to recruit Help Desk Engineers. The following is the selection criteria. The candidates must\\n(i) be a diploma holder or an Engineer.\\n(ii) be an Engineer with at least 60% marks or a diploma holder with at least 70% marks.\\n(iii) have experience in hardware engineering, and networking.\\n(iv) have an aptitude for troubleshooting of desktops / palmtops / laptops.\\n(v) have at least two years of similar experience in a BPO.\\n(vi) have excellent communication skills in English.\\n(vii) be willing to work in shifts.\\n\\nHowever, if a candidate fulfils all other criteria except\\n(P) (ii) but has over five years of similar experience in a BPO, then he/she is referred to the Chief Operating Officer.\\n(Q) (v) but has a consistent academic performance of more than 75%, he/she is to be considered for the post of Trainee Help Desk Engineer.\\n\\nBased on the above criteria and information provided about each candidate, take a decision in each case. You are not to assume anything. If the data given is not adequate to take a decision, mark your answer as data inadequate. Give answer\\n(A) if the candidate is selected as an Help Desk Engineer.\\n(B) if the candidate is referred to the Chief Operating Officer.\\n(C) if the candidate is selected as a Trainee Help Desk Engineer.\\n(D) if the data is inadequate.","setup_solution":"Each candidate is checked against criteria (i)-(vii). This section's answer key has no dedicated 'rejected' code; candidates who fail a criterion with no matching exception, or where the exception's wording is not clearly satisfied, are treated as data inadequate (D) since none of A/B/C can be confidently assigned.","entity_count":8,"variables":[],"constraints":[],"case_splits":[],"resolution_type":"rule_based_decision","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["criteria_checklist_evaluation","exception_handling","data_sufficiency_analysis"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E20_Q017","question_text":"Asra Das completed her Engineering with 65% marks and has experience in hardware engineering and networking. She has very good communication skills in English and is willing to work in shifts. She has three years of similar experience in a BPO and an aptitude for troubleshooting of laptops.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","solution_text":"Engineer with 65%>=60% (ii). Hardware engineering and networking experience (iii). Aptitude for laptops, one of desktops/palmtops/laptops (iv). 3 years similar BPO experience >=2 (v). Excellent English (vi). Willing to work in shifts (vii). Is an Engineer (i). All 7 criteria satisfied -> Selected as Help Desk Engineer.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q018","question_text":"Sanjay, a diploma holder with 76% of marks, has experience in hardware engineering and has an aptitude for desktop trouble shooting. He has a similar work experience in a BPO for the last four years and has excellent communication skills in English. He is willing to work in shifts.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Diploma holder with 76%>=70% (ii). Aptitude for desktops (iv). 4 years similar BPO experience >=2 (v). Excellent English (vi). Willing shifts (vii). Diploma holder (i). However, condition (iii) requires experience in BOTH hardware engineering AND networking; only hardware engineering experience is stated, networking is never mentioned. Since (iii) has no exception clause, if he lacks networking experience he cannot be selected, but if he has it he is selected outright - these are different outcomes, so this is data inadequate.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120,"type_specific":{"note":"This section's options provide no direct 'rejected' code; where a candidate clearly fails with no exception, or an exception's exact wording is ambiguous, D (data inadequate) is used as the best available fit rather than force-fitting A/B/C."}},{"id":"LR_E20_Q019","question_text":"Akash Menon is a fresh Engineering graduate with a consistent academic performance of above 80%. He has experience in hardware engineering and networking. He has an aptitude for troubleshooting of palmtops. He is willing to work in shifts. He has excellent communication skills in English.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","solution_text":"Engineer with consistent academic performance >80%>=60% (ii). Hardware engineering and networking (iii). Aptitude for palmtops (iv). Excellent English (vi). Willing shifts (vii). Is an Engineer (i). Being a 'fresh' graduate means he fails the >=2 years BPO experience requirement (v). Exception Q: fails (v) alone, but has consistent academic performance >75% (>80% here) -> considered for Trainee Help Desk Engineer.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q020","question_text":"Ravi, a Engineering graduate with more than 55% marks, who has experience in networking and hardware engineering is very good at English communications. He has an aptitude for troubleshooting of laptops and he has three years similar experience in a BPO. He is willing to work in shifts.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Networking and hardware engineering (iii). Aptitude for laptops (iv). 3 years similar BPO experience >=2 (v). Excellent English (vi). Willing shifts (vii). Is an Engineer (i). But his marks are only stated as 'more than 55%', which does not confirm whether he meets the required 60% for an Engineer (ii). If >=60%, he is selected outright. If between 55-60%, condition (ii) fails; exception P requires over 5 years similar BPO experience, but he only has 3 years, so exception P would not apply, and he could not be selected. Since these are different outcomes, this is data inadequate.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120,"type_specific":{"note":"This section's options provide no direct 'rejected' code; where a candidate clearly fails with no exception, or an exception's exact wording is ambiguous, D (data inadequate) is used as the best available fit rather than force-fitting A/B/C."}},{"id":"LR_E20_Q021","question_text":"Smriti, an Engineering graduate with 52% marks, has experience in networking and hardware engineering. She has an aptitude for trouble shooting of desk tops and has similar experience in a BPO for six years. She is willing to work in shifts and she has excellent communication skills in English.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","solution_text":"Networking and hardware engineering (iii). Aptitude for desktops (iv). 6 years similar BPO experience >=2 (v). Excellent English (vi). Willing shifts (vii). Is an Engineer (i). Engineer with 52%<60% fails (ii). Exception P: fails (ii) alone, but has over 5 years similar BPO experience (6>5) -> referred to Chief Operating Officer.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q022","question_text":"Gargi who has excellent communication skills in English, is a diploma holder with 80% marks. He has experience in hardware engineering and networking. He has an aptitude for troubleshooting in laptops and has one year of similar experience in a BPO. He is willing to work in any shift.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Diploma holder with 80%>=70% (ii). Hardware engineering and networking (iii). Aptitude laptops (iv). Excellent English (vi). Willing shifts (vii). Diploma holder (i). Only 1 year similar BPO experience fails the >=2 year requirement (v). Exception Q requires a 'consistent academic performance' of more than 75%; here only a bare diploma percentage (80%) is stated, not phrased as a consistent academic record, so exception Q's specific wording is not clearly satisfied. Given this section provides no explicit 'rejected' answer code, this candidate's outcome could not be confidently mapped to Selected/COO/Trainee, so this is flagged data inadequate rather than force-fit.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120,"type_specific":{"note":"This section's options provide no direct 'rejected' code; where a candidate clearly fails with no exception, or an exception's exact wording is ambiguous, D (data inadequate) is used as the best available fit rather than force-fitting A/B/C."}},{"id":"LR_E20_Q023","question_text":"Garima, an engineering graduate with 70% marks, has excellent communication skills in English. She is willing to work in shifts and has over three years of similar experience in a BPO. She has an experience in networking and hardware engineering and aptitude for troubleshooting of desktops.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","solution_text":"Engineer with 70%>=60% (ii). Excellent English (vi). Willing shifts (vii). Over 3 years similar BPO experience >=2 (v). Networking and hardware engineering (iii). Aptitude desktops (iv). Is an Engineer (i). All 7 criteria satisfied -> Selected as Help Desk Engineer.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q024","question_text":"Chauhan, an engineering graduate with 65% marks, has excellent communication skills in English. He is willing to work in shifts and has over three years of similar experience. He has experience in hardware engineering and networking and has an aptitude for troubleshooting of laptops.","options":{"A":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","B":"Referred to Chief Operating Officer","C":"Selected as Trainee Help Desk Engineer","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected as Help Desk Engineer","solution_text":"Engineer with 65%>=60% (ii). Excellent English (vi). Willing shifts (vii). Over 3 years 'similar experience' - read as similar BPO experience consistent with the pattern of surrounding questions, >=2 (v). Hardware engineering and networking (iii). Aptitude laptops (iv). Is an Engineer (i). All 7 criteria satisfied -> Selected as Help Desk Engineer.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E20_S25_32","exercise":"exercise_1","type":"selection_criteria_decision","is_set":true,"setup_text":"Directions for questions 25 to 32: Study the following information carefully and answer the questions given below.\\n\\n'SMILE' an international developmental organization working in different parts of India focussing on the eradication of child labour is looking for a national coordinator for a project. The following is the selection criteria. The candidate must\\n(i) have Master's degree in Social Sciences/Economics/Development studies.\\n(ii) have a minimum of 8 years of work experience in development field.\\n(iii) have at least 5 years of research experience.\\n(iv) have excellent understanding of macro-economic policies.\\n(v) be self motivated and a team player.\\n\\nHowever, if a candidate fulfils all other criteria except\\n(P) (iii) above but has at least 5 years of experience as a project manager then he is referred to the Director, SMILE.\\n(Q) (iv) above but has a doctoral degree in social service, then he is referred to the Chairman, SMILE.\\n\\nBased on the above criteria and information provided about each candidate take a decision in each case. You are not to assume anything. If the data given is not adequate to take a decision mark your answer as 'Data inadequate'. Give answers\\n(A) if the candidate is selected as a National Coordinator.\\n(B) if the candidate is referred to the Director or Chairman, SMILE.\\n(C) if the data is inadequate.\\n(D) if the candidate is rejected.","setup_solution":"Each candidate is checked against criteria (i)-(v). If exactly one of (iii) or (iv) fails, the corresponding exception (P/Q) is checked. If two or more criteria fail simultaneously, no exception applies. Missing data on a no-exception criterion (v) that could change the outcome makes the answer data inadequate.","entity_count":8,"variables":[],"constraints":[],"case_splits":[],"resolution_type":"rule_based_decision","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["criteria_checklist_evaluation","exception_handling","data_sufficiency_analysis"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E20_Q025","question_text":"Vikas has Masters degree in Economics and has an excellent understanding of macroeconomic policies. He has ten years of work experience in the development field and six years of work experience in research. He is self motivated and an excellent team player.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Selected as National Coordinator","solution_text":"Master's in Economics (i). Excellent macro-economic understanding (iv). 10 years development field experience >=8 (ii). 6 years research experience >=5 (iii). Self motivated and team player (v). All 5 criteria satisfied -> Selected as National Coordinator.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q026","question_text":"Pankaj Pandey has done his Master's degree in Social Sciences and has an experience of over ten years in the development field and is a project manager for six years. He also has one year experience in research. He is self motivated and a team player and has an excellent understanding of macroeconomic policies.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","solution_text":"Master's in Social Sciences (i). Over 10 years development field experience >=8 (ii). Excellent macro-economic understanding (iv). Self motivated, team player (v). Only 1 year of research experience fails the >=5 year requirement (iii). Exception P: fails (iii) alone, but has >=5 years experience as a project manager (6>=5) -> referred to the Director, SMILE.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q027","question_text":"Yoginder is self motivated and a team player and has a Master's degree in Development studies. He has over nine years of experience in the development field out of which three years of experience is in research and he worked as a project manager for 4 years. He has excellent understanding of macro economic polices.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Rejected","solution_text":"Self motivated, team player (v). Master's in Development studies (i). Over 9 years development field experience >=8 (ii). Excellent macro-economic understanding (iv). Only 3 years research experience fails the >=5 year requirement (iii). Exception P requires >=5 years as project manager, but he has only 4 years -> exception P does not apply -> Rejected.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q028","question_text":"Shilpibali has over twelve years of experience in the development field out of which seven years is in research. She has Master's degree in Economics and an excellent understanding of microeconomic policies. She is self motivated and a team player.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Rejected","solution_text":"Over 12 years development field experience >=8 (ii). 7 years research experience >=5 (iii). Master's in Economics (i). Self motivated, team player (v). Her understanding is of MICRO-economic policies, not macro-economic policies as required by (iv) - these are different subjects, so (iv) fails. Exception Q requires a doctoral degree in social service, which is not stated -> exception Q does not apply -> Rejected.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q029","question_text":"Parimala, has Master's degree in Social Sciences and a Doctoral degree in Social Service. She has nine years of experience in development field out of which six years is in research. She is self motivated and a team player. She has no understanding of macroeconomic policies.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","solution_text":"Master's in Social Sciences (i). 9 years development field experience >=8 (ii). 6 years research experience >=5 (iii). Self motivated, team player (v). She has no understanding of macroeconomic policies, failing (iv) alone. Exception Q: fails (iv) alone, but has a doctoral degree in social service (yes) -> referred to the Chairman, SMILE.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q030","question_text":"Rajesh has over eleven years of experience in development filed out of which six years is in research. He has an excellent understanding of macro economic policies. He has Master's degree in Economics.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Over 11 years development field experience >=8 (ii). 6 years research experience >=5 (iii). Excellent macro-economic understanding (iv). Master's in Economics (i). Whether he is self motivated and a team player (v) is never stated, and (v) has no exception clause. If he is, he is selected (A); if not, he is rejected (D). These are different codes, so this is data inadequate.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q031","question_text":"Shruti has done her Master's degree in Economics and has an experience of over twelve years in development field out of which 4 years is in research. She has no understanding of macroeconomic policies. She is a self motivated and a team player.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Rejected","solution_text":"Master's in Economics (i). Over 12 years development field experience >=8 (ii). Self motivated, team player (v). She fails BOTH (iii) (only 4 years research, needs >=5) AND (iv) (no understanding of macroeconomic policies) simultaneously. Since the exceptions P and Q each require failing only ONE specific condition, and here two conditions fail at once, neither exception can apply -> Rejected.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E20_Q032","question_text":"Joseph has nine years of experience in development field out of which 5 years experience is in research. She has no understanding of macroeconomic policies. He is self motivated and a team player. He has Master's degree in Social Sciences and also has a Doctoral degree in Social Service.","options":{"A":"Selected as National Coordinator","B":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Rejected"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Referred to Director or Chairman, SMILE","solution_text":"Master's in Social Sciences (i). 9 years development field experience >=8 (ii). 5 years research experience meets the 'at least 5 years' threshold exactly (iii). Self motivated, team player (v). No understanding of macroeconomic policies fails (iv) alone. Exception Q: fails (iv) alone, has a doctoral degree in social service (yes) -> referred to the Chairman, SMILE.","question_operation":"evaluate_selection_criteria","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E20_S33_40","exercise":"exercise_1","type":"number_classification_rules","is_set":true,"setup_text":"Directions for questions 33 to 40: These questions are based on the following information. A number classifying machine classifies a given number as 'Sensible number' if the number has (i) at least six digits, (ii) at least two even digits, (iii) a prime number in the units place and (iv) no two digits are same. If a given number satisfies all the criteria except, (P) (ii) alone, but starts with an even digit, then the number is classified as 'Soft number'. (Q) (iii) alone, but the number is odd then the number is classified as 'Difficult number'. (R) (iv) alone, but no two consecutive digits are the same then the numbers is classified as 'Complicated number'. If a number does not fit into any of the above mentioned classification, then the number is classified as 'Waste number'. Based on the above mentioned criteria decide the classification for the numbers given in the questions. Mark your answer as. (A) if the number is classified as Sensible number or Waste number. (B) if the number is classified as Soft number. (C) if the number is classified as Difficult number. (D) if the number is classified as Complicated number.","setup_solution":"Single-digit primes are 2,3,5,7. Each number is checked against (i)-(iv) in order; if exactly one of (ii),(iii),(iv) fails, the corresponding exception is checked using its own specific sub-condition.","entity_count":8,"variables":[],"constraints":[],"case_splits":[],"resolution_type":"rule_based_classification","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["digit_analysis","primality_check","exception_handling"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E20_Q033","question_text":"4687322","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Sensible number/Waste number","solution_text":"Digits 4,6,8,7,3,2,2 = 7 digits (>=6, i). Even digits: 4,6,8,2,2 = 5 (>=2, ii). Units digit 2 is prime (iii). Digit '2' repeats (positions 6,7) failing all-distinct (iv). Exception R needs no two CONSECUTIVE digits equal, but the two 2's are adjacent (...3,2,2) so they ARE consecutive -> exception R fails -> Waste number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E20_Q034","question_text":"3456789","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Difficult number","solution_text":"Digits 3,4,5,6,7,8,9 = 7 digits (i). Even digits 4,6,8 = 3 (>=2, ii). Units digit 9 is not prime, failing (iii). Number is odd (ends in 9). All digits distinct (iv). Exception Q: fails (iii) alone, number is odd -> Difficult number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E20_Q035","question_text":"138642","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Sensible number/Waste number","solution_text":"Digits 1,3,8,6,4,2 = 6 digits (i, exactly minimum). Even digits 8,6,4,2 = 4 (>=2, ii). Units digit 2 is prime (iii). All digits distinct (iv). All four conditions satisfied -> Sensible number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E20_Q036","question_text":"291735","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Soft number","solution_text":"Digits 2,9,1,7,3,5 = 6 digits (i). Only one even digit (2), failing the >=2 requirement (ii). Units digit 5 is prime (iii). All digits distinct (iv). Exception P: fails (ii) alone, and starts with an even digit (first digit is 2) -> Soft number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E20_Q037","question_text":"85613","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Sensible number/Waste number","solution_text":"Digits 8,5,6,1,3 = only 5 digits, failing the at-least-6-digit requirement (i). Condition (i) has no exception -> falls through to Waste number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E20_Q038","question_text":"9713864","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Sensible number/Waste number","solution_text":"Digits 9,7,1,3,8,6,4 = 7 digits (i). Even digits 8,6,4 = 3 (>=2, ii). Units digit 4 is not prime, failing (iii). The number is even (ends in 4), not odd, so exception Q ('fails iii alone but is odd') does not apply -> Waste number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E20_Q039","question_text":"2976813","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Sensible number/Waste number","solution_text":"Digits 2,9,7,6,8,1,3 = 7 digits (i). Even digits 2,6,8 = 3 (>=2, ii). Units digit 3 is prime (iii). All digits distinct (iv). All four conditions satisfied -> Sensible number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E20_Q040","question_text":"5796723","options":{"A":"Sensible number/Waste number","B":"Soft number","C":"Difficult number","D":"Complicated number"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Complicated number","solution_text":"Digits 5,7,9,6,7,2,3 = 7 digits (i). Even digits 6,2 = 2 (>=2, ii, exactly minimum). Units digit 3 is prime (iii). Digit '7' repeats (positions 2 and 5), failing all-distinct (iv). Checking all adjacent pairs (5,7)(7,9)(9,6)(6,7)(7,2)(2,3), no two consecutive digits are equal, satisfying exception R's specific condition -> Complicated number.","question_operation":"classify_number","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E20_S41_45","exercise":"exercise_1","type":"flowchart_decision","is_set":true,"set_image":"QIMG_LR_E20_S41_45","wide_reference":true,"setup_text":"Directions for questions 41 to 45: The following are the criteria for organizing the Training Programme in different hotels. The following flow chart represents the criteria and steps involved in allotting different Hotels to organize the Training Programme based on the information provided.","setup_solution":"Flowchart routing (as read from the image): (1) participants>=50 AND duration<=7days, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (2) area in {Advertising, Computers, Statistics}, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (3) coordinator is Joint Director, YES-> (8) fee>=7000 [YES-> Hotel Taj, NO-> falls through to (x)]; (3) NO-> (4) coordinator is Assistant Director, NO-> No Hotel allotted, YES-> (5) participants>=80 AND duration>=4days, YES-> (6) fee>=5000 [YES-> Hotel Saucy, NO-> falls through to (x)], NO(from 5)-> falls through to (8); (x) fee>=3500, YES-> Hotel Ritz, NO-> No Hotel allotted.","entity_count":5,"variables":[],"constraints":[],"case_splits":[],"resolution_type":"flowchart_traversal","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["flowchart_tracing","conditional_gate_evaluation","data_sufficiency_analysis"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E20_Q041","question_text":"A 5-day training programme for 55 participants is to be organized by Shri Jairam Singh, the Assistant Director. The fee of the participant is 4500.","options":{"A":"Hotel Taj","B":"Hotel Ritz","C":"Hotel Saucy","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Flowchart routing (as read from the image): (1) participants>=50 AND duration<=7days, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (2) area in {Advertising, Computers, Statistics}, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (3) coordinator is Joint Director, YES-> (8) fee>=7000 [YES-> Hotel Taj, NO-> falls through to (x)]; (3) NO-> (4) coordinator is Assistant Director, NO-> No Hotel allotted, YES-> (5) participants>=80 AND duration>=4days, YES-> (6) fee>=5000 [YES-> Hotel Saucy, NO-> falls through to (x)], NO(from 5)-> falls through to (8); (x) fee>=3500, YES-> Hotel Ritz, NO-> No Hotel allotted. For this candidate: (1) 55>=50 and 5<=7, YES. Coordinator is Assistant Director (not Joint Director), so path goes (3)NO->(4)YES->(5): 55>=80 is FALSE, so (5)=NO, falling through to (8): fee 4500>=7000 is FALSE, falling through to (x): fee 4500>=3500 is TRUE -> Hotel Ritz. However, the programme's subject area (needed at gate (2)) is never stated. If the area is NOT one of Advertising/Computers/Statistics, gate (2) fails and the outcome is 'No Hotel allotted' instead of Ritz. Since these are genuinely different outcomes depending on the missing area data, this is data inadequate.","question_operation":"trace_flowchart","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150,"type_specific":{"note":"Verified against the actual flowchart image: the fee-fallback routing (a failed high-fee gate falling through to the lower fee gate) is confirmed correct. The core issue for this question is the missing programme area, which creates genuine divergence between a Ritz assignment and outright rejection."}},{"id":"LR_E20_Q042","question_text":"A training programme on Advertising is to be organized by Shri Tiwari, the Joint Director, for 78 participants and fee per participant is 6000 and the duration of the course is 6 days.","options":{"A":"Hotel Ritz","B":"No Hotel allotted","C":"Hotel Saucy","D":"Hotel Taj"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Hotel Ritz","solution_text":"Flowchart routing (as read from the image): (1) participants>=50 AND duration<=7days, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (2) area in {Advertising, Computers, Statistics}, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (3) coordinator is Joint Director, YES-> (8) fee>=7000 [YES-> Hotel Taj, NO-> falls through to (x)]; (3) NO-> (4) coordinator is Assistant Director, NO-> No Hotel allotted, YES-> (5) participants>=80 AND duration>=4days, YES-> (6) fee>=5000 [YES-> Hotel Saucy, NO-> falls through to (x)], NO(from 5)-> falls through to (8); (x) fee>=3500, YES-> Hotel Ritz, NO-> No Hotel allotted. (1) 78>=50 and 6<=7, YES. (2) Advertising is a valid area, YES. (3) Joint Director, YES -> (8): fee 6000>=7000 is FALSE, falling through to (x): fee 6000>=3500 is TRUE -> Hotel Ritz.","question_operation":"trace_flowchart","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150,"type_specific":{"note":"Verified against the actual flowchart image: the fee-check fallback (a failed 'Fee>=7000' check falling through to 'Fee>=3500') is confirmed correct."}},{"id":"LR_E20_Q043","question_text":"Dr. Saroja Devi, Joint Director of the institute wants to organize a programme for 100 students with duration of the course for 5 days in the area of Computers. The fee per participant is 8500.","options":{"A":"Hotel Ritz","B":"Data inadequate","C":"Hotel Taj","D":"Hotel Saucy"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Hotel Taj","solution_text":"Flowchart routing (as read from the image): (1) participants>=50 AND duration<=7days, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (2) area in {Advertising, Computers, Statistics}, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (3) coordinator is Joint Director, YES-> (8) fee>=7000 [YES-> Hotel Taj, NO-> falls through to (x)]; (3) NO-> (4) coordinator is Assistant Director, NO-> No Hotel allotted, YES-> (5) participants>=80 AND duration>=4days, YES-> (6) fee>=5000 [YES-> Hotel Saucy, NO-> falls through to (x)], NO(from 5)-> falls through to (8); (x) fee>=3500, YES-> Hotel Ritz, NO-> No Hotel allotted. (1) 100>=50 and 5<=7, YES. (2) Computers is a valid area, YES. (3) Joint Director, YES -> (8): fee 8500>=7000 is TRUE -> Hotel Taj.","question_operation":"trace_flowchart","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E20_Q044","question_text":"Prof. Sunil Kumar, Assistant Director, has offered 4 days programme for 93 students in the area of Advertising. The fee per participant is 5500.","options":{"A":"Hotel Saucy","B":"Data inadequate","C":"No Hotel allotted","D":"Hotel Ritz"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Hotel Saucy","solution_text":"Flowchart routing (as read from the image): (1) participants>=50 AND duration<=7days, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (2) area in {Advertising, Computers, Statistics}, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (3) coordinator is Joint Director, YES-> (8) fee>=7000 [YES-> Hotel Taj, NO-> falls through to (x)]; (3) NO-> (4) coordinator is Assistant Director, NO-> No Hotel allotted, YES-> (5) participants>=80 AND duration>=4days, YES-> (6) fee>=5000 [YES-> Hotel Saucy, NO-> falls through to (x)], NO(from 5)-> falls through to (8); (x) fee>=3500, YES-> Hotel Ritz, NO-> No Hotel allotted. (1) 93>=50 and 4<=7, YES. (2) Advertising is a valid area, YES. (3) not Joint Director -> (4) Assistant Director, YES -> (5): 93>=80 TRUE and duration 4>=4 TRUE, so (5)=YES -> (6): fee 5500>=5000 is TRUE -> Hotel Saucy.","question_operation":"trace_flowchart","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E20_Q045","question_text":"A training programme on statistics is proposed by Dr. Vinod Raj, the Assistant Director, for 3 days on Advertising. The number of participants is 85 and the fee per participant is 5800.","options":{"A":"Hotel Saucy","B":"No Hotel allotted","C":"Data inadequate","D":"Hotel Taj"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Data inadequate","solution_text":"Flowchart routing (as read from the image): (1) participants>=50 AND duration<=7days, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (2) area in {Advertising, Computers, Statistics}, NO-> No Hotel allotted; YES-> (3) coordinator is Joint Director, YES-> (8) fee>=7000 [YES-> Hotel Taj, NO-> falls through to (x)]; (3) NO-> (4) coordinator is Assistant Director, NO-> No Hotel allotted, YES-> (5) participants>=80 AND duration>=4days, YES-> (6) fee>=5000 [YES-> Hotel Saucy, NO-> falls through to (x)], NO(from 5)-> falls through to (8); (x) fee>=3500, YES-> Hotel Ritz, NO-> No Hotel allotted. The programme's area is stated inconsistently as both 'on statistics' and 'on Advertising' in the same sentence - a genuine contradiction in the given data (though it happens not to matter at gate (2), since both are valid areas). Working the flowchart mechanically: (1) 85>=50 and 3<=7, YES; (2) area valid, YES; (3) not Joint Director -> (4) Assistant Director, YES -> (5): 85>=80 TRUE but duration 3>=4 FALSE, so (5)=NO, falling through to (8): fee 5800>=7000 FALSE, falling through to (x): fee 5800>=3500 TRUE, which would mechanically give Hotel Ritz - but Hotel Ritz is not even offered as an option here, which signals that this question is testing whether the contradictory/unreliable area description is recognized as a data-quality problem rather than being resolved mechanically. Given the self-contradictory area statement, data inadequate is the answer.","question_operation":"trace_flowchart","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150,"type_specific":{"note":"Hotel Ritz is not among this question's answer options even though a mechanical trace of the flowchart would land there; this is presented as data inadequate based on the self-contradictory area description ('on statistics' and 'on Advertising' in the same sentence), which is judged to be the intended source of ambiguity rather than the flowchart routing itself."}}]}]`);export{e as default};
